tShell"},"name":"Reviews inbox: thread timeline","spec":{"accessibility":["The timeline is an ordered list named \"Thread history\"; each entry has an icon and words, never color alone, and a dismissal reads \"Dismissed\" with its kind.","The Evidence disclosure is a button that exposes whether it is open; copy buttons are named by what they copy."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Stack, Text, Badge, Icon, Button, TimelineItem, Disclosure); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","Message editing, the edited marker and the edit history are in the thread bubble Views of the Comments slice; the copy buttons of the real timeline are icon buttons here without their feedback.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; names, ids and digests bind through value and value2 and a sentence the app builds from translated pieces is one sample string per Locale. en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member opened a thread in the Reviews pane, sheet or slide-over; the timeline is derived from the thread (its messages, submissions and history events), never stored on its own.","The base state is a message from a reviewer and an Agent's answer followed by the submission that is ready for review; Variants add the submission's Evidence, a verified or answered resolution, a dismissal that leaves the submission not accepted, a reopening and a re-anchor.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the strings follow the Workbench language and names, ids, digests and change domains are literal identities."],"intent":"Show the timeline of a Review thread as the Reviews inbox reads it: the messages, the submissions with their state, change domains, Evidence and id, the resolutions (verified, answered, dismissed), the reopenings and the re-anchors, in the order they happened.","interactionRules":["One chronological list shows each entry with its own look: a message with its author (an Agent is marked) and time; a submission, its state (Current, Accepted or Not accepted), the change domains it names, an Evidence count that opens the digests and a link to the View's Readiness, and its id; a resolution as a chip with who resolved and when, plus the reason when one was given; a reopening with its reason; a re-anchor from one target to another, with the Variant scope change when it moved.","Verified names the submission it accepts; any other resolution of a ready-for-review thread leaves the pending submission in the thread, marked Not accepted. A dismissal is neutral, never green.","Reopening a thread, whatever its resolution, keeps every earlier event and submission as it was."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"468247e8-4f39-4f04-8056-b2af4c1c37ea"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a104-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a04"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"c6c0a101-7b3e-4d19-8a26-3e9d1c0b6a01"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a101-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a01"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a102-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a02"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a103-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a03"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a104-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a04"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"e1b7a106-4c2d-4e3f-9a5b-6d7c8e9f0a06"}],"requirements":["01a11544-53e8-75b3-b819-d86993a21069","01a11544-5459-73a9-89d2-dd4d3ed42da3"]},"variants":{"accepted-verified":{"requirements":["01a11544-5702-78b6-95ea-c15fe80ad4e3"],"state":{"res-verified":{"visible":true},"sub-accepted":{"visible":true},"sub-current":{"visible":false}}},"answered":{"state":